  "body": "Found during #1842.\n\n## What happens\n\nWith \"Threading: G76 cycle\" and a flank infeed, the Fanuc lathe post writes one G76 cycle. Two published manuals show that the control ends every pass at the programmed end point D:\n\n- FANUC Series 0i-F lathe operator's manual B-64604EN-1, section 4.2.7, Fig. 4.2.7 (a).\n- Siemens SINUMERIK ISO Turning programming manual A5E52211627B, Fig. 4-25.\n\nThe turning kernel (`crates/motion/src/turning/thread.rs`, the pass loop) shifts the start AND the end of each pass by the same flank offset. Thus a shallower pass ends short of D by `(k - depth) * tan(a/2)`. Only the root pass ends at D.\n\n## Effect\n\nThe control cuts each shallower pass a little longer than the laid pass that the verdict and the stock simulation see. The extra length is at a smaller depth, inside the groove that the root pass cuts to D. It removes no material beyond the root pass and does not move toward a shoulder. Thus this is not a wrong-output defect. But the simulated passes are not exactly the passes that run.\n\n`crates/app/tests/lathe_post_g76_sources.rs::every_pass_runs_to_the_posted_end_z_inside_the_root_pass` pins the present difference.\n\n## Done means\n\nOne of these:\n\n- The kernel lays each flank pass of a G76-postable plan to the same end station, and the pin changes to assert that.\n- Or a decision records why the present laid ends stay.\n",
